<title>UK: Abacus Polar weak after franchise deal ends.</title>
<headline>Abacus Polar weak after franchise deal ends.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in electronics component distributor Abacus Polar dropped sharply on Thursday, after the company said its franchise agreement with Microchip Technology Inc. was being terminated from November.</p>
<p>Abacus Polar headed losers in mid-morning trade as its shares dropped 25p or more than 15 percent to 139p by 0937 GMT. Some 40,000 shares had changed hands by that time.</p>
<p>Abacus said Microchip accounted for four percent of group turnover in the first nine months of this year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
